Seam: chrome/BUILD.gn, mac_app_bundle("chrome_app"), its deps.
Why: the updater is a framework that has to sit inside the application, in
     Contents/Frameworks beside Chromium's own, and only the application
     target decides what the bundle holds. The dependency is a group that is
     empty unless the build is official, so only a release carries Sparkle
     and a development build never offers to replace itself with a published
     one.
Delegates to: nothing. This patch carries no call -- it is GN wiring to the
     group in arcium/browser/update/BUILD.gn that names the framework.

diff --git a/chrome/BUILD.gn b/chrome/BUILD.gn
--- a/chrome/BUILD.gn
+++ b/chrome/BUILD.gn
@@ -548,6 +548,7 @@ if (is_win) {
       ":chrome_app_strings_bundle_data",
       ":chrome_resources",
       ":chrome_versioned_bundle_data",
+      "//arcium/browser/update:sparkle_in_bundle",
       "//base:compiler_specific",
       "//base/allocator:early_zone_registration_apple",
       "//build:branding_buildflags",
